plementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions).\n\nPair list for `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/`, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment. Format: `base | heldout LOC | RENAME (differing defs)`; the twin is `<base>_heldout.py`. No test-function name collides in these pairs; definitions that collide with DIFFERENT bodies are named in the RENAME column (rename on merge); every other colliding definition is identical (dedupe: keep the base copy; `pytestmark` counts here).\n\n`tests/integration/` — 1 pair, 0 renames:\n\n| # | base | heldout LOC | RENAME (differing defs) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py` | 421 | - |\n\n`tests/interfaces/` — 16 pairs, 5 renames:\n\n| # | base | heldout LOC | RENAME (differing defs) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llmrunner_error_codes_f75f.py` | 102 | - |\n| 3 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli.py` | 463 | - |\n| 4 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py` | 215 | - |\n| 5 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status.py` | 276 | `_plant_blob`, `_run_cli` |\n| 6 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary.py` | 176 | - |\n| 7 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_detected_by.py` | 212 | `_create_data` |\n| 8 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope.py` | 244 | - |\n| 9 | `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck.py` | 236 | `_make` |\n| 10 | `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_bug_close_class.py` | 73 | - |\n| 11 | `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_autoderive.py` | 53 | - |\n| 12 | `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_relation.py` | 91 | - |\n| 13 | `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py` | 146 | `_commit_ref` (base docstring cites bug ferric-jet-scorpion; it stays the base docstring) |\n| 14 | `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py` | 79 | - |\n| 15 | `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_stale_channel_repair.py` | 239 | - |\n| 16 | `tests/interfaces/test_metrics_cli.py` | 77 | `_cli` |\n| 17 | `tests/interfaces/test_metrics_polyglot.py` | 57 | - |\n\n17 pairs; 5 renames = rows 5, 7, 9, 13, 16.\n\nRename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_plant_blob_heldout`, `_run_cli_heldout`, `_make_heldout`) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions.\n\nMerge recipe per pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (incl. `pytestmark`); rename differing definitions with the `_heldout` suffix and repoint callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Record per pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before, `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after (row 1 under `-m integration`).\n\nNot in this story: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py` (unpaired; it receives E10a-S1's moved tests and is renamed in S5) and `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py` (cross-tier twin of `tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py`; S5 renames it to `test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`; do not merge across tiers).","timestamp":1788807536242290670}],"created_at":1788807278200952377,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n17 modules under `tests/interfaces/` (16 pairs: 1 in `contracts/`, 6 in `facades/`, 6 in `lifecycle/`, 1 in `store/`, 2 at the directory root) and `tests/integration/` (1 pair, `test_s3_doctor.py`) have a `<name>_heldout.py` twin. Once both oracles have been reviewed the split only doubles module count, duplicates identical helper definitions, and makes every rename touch two files. Across these 17 pairs no test-function name collides; 5 pairs carry helper definitions with differing bodies and every other colliding definition is identical. The pair list with per-pair rename sets, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\nDirectories: `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` — 17 pairs, 5 renames (`test_bridge_status`, `test_detected_by`, `test_ac_checkbox_precheck`, `test_close_gate_subtree`, `test_metrics_cli`). For each pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (`pytestmark` counts here — keep the base copy); rename differing definitions and repoint their callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Rename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_load_heldout`) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions. `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py` cites bug ferric-jet-scorpion in its docstring; that docstring stays the base docstring. No test body changes.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 17 base modules under `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` named in the first comment and their 17 `_heldout` twins. Out of scope: the `tests/unit/` pairs (S1, S2), `tests/scripts/` (S4), the 78 unpaired held-out renames (S5) — including `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py` and `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py`, which have no base twin in this directory — every file under `src/`, and any test body change.\n\n## Testing\nPer pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after — counts equal (both recorded on this ticket); `pytest <base>` green (the `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py` pair runs under `-m integration`). `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Zero paired twins remain in these directories: for each of the 17 pairs `git ls-files <base>_heldout.py` prints nothing (the unpaired `_heldout` modules in these directories are untouched here and renamed in S5).\n- [ ] Per-pair node counts reconcile: each merged base collects exactly the sum of the two prior counts, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` shows `new=0` (no autouse fixture lives in these pairs).\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llmrunner_error_codes_f75f.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llmrunner_error_codes_f75f_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_detected_by.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_detected_by_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope.py","reason":"merge heldout twin"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope_heldout.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck.py","reason":"merge 